== 1.7 Chapter 1 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

#block(sticky: true)[Allow 44 minutes. Answer all items before checking the key; read every explanation.]

#mcq(1, [The WHO constitutional definition describes health as], [absence of infection alone], [a single laboratory result], [physical, mental and social wellbeing, not merely absence of disease], [physical fitness alone])

#mcq(2, [Belonging and supportive relationships are most directly associated with], [bone density], [joint range], [pulse rate], [social wellbeing])

#mcq(3, [Managing emotions and seeking support are most directly associated with], [mental wellbeing], [a tournament draw], [a throwing technique], [a bone classification])

#mcq(4, [Which statement about health dimensions is sound?], [A single symptom measures all dimensions], [They interact and can change over time], [They are completely independent], [Social wellbeing is always determined by fitness])

#mcq(5, [A person living with a chronic condition], [can be assessed completely from appearance], [cannot experience wellbeing in any dimension], [can still experience wellbeing and participate in community life], [must be excluded from all activities])

#mcq(6, [Personal hygiene refers to], [competition rules], [a complete medical diagnosis], [practices that help keep the body clean and reduce certain risks], [a guarantee of lifelong immunity])

#mcq(7, [Before preparing food, a useful hygiene practice is to], [use the same unwashed hands after the toilet], [assume food handling cannot transfer germs], [ignore visible dirt], [wash hands with soap and clean running water])

#mcq(8, [After using the toilet, hands should ideally be washed with], [water previously used for bathing], [a dry cloth alone], [soap and clean running water], [no water or soap])

#mcq(9, [When soap and water are unavailable, an alternative hand rub should contain at least], [40% alcohol], [6% alcohol], [60% alcohol], [16% alcohol])

#mcq(10, [Hand sanitizer may be less effective when hands are], [clean and dry before use], [visibly dirty or greasy], [covered completely with sanitizer], [rubbed until dry])

#mcq(11, [A useful handwashing action is to], [rub all hand surfaces with soap before rinsing], [wash only one hand], [rinse only fingertips without soap], [dry hands before applying soap])

#mcq(12, [Personal hygiene measures], [replace all vaccination and healthcare], [reduce some risks but cannot guarantee freedom from illness], [prove a person has no infection], [prevent every illness in every case])

#mcq(13, [Oral care commonly includes], [using any unverified remedy instead of assessment], [brushing with fluoride toothpaste and obtaining dental advice when needed], [assuming tooth pain never needs attention], [avoiding all tooth cleaning])

#mcq(14, [Good menstrual hygiene requires attention to], [shame and exclusion], [avoiding all discussion or support], [clean materials, privacy and safe disposal], [identical facilities in every setting regardless of access])

#mcq(15, [A school teaches handwashing but supplies no water. Which barrier remains?], [lack of access to a necessary resource], [automatic immunity to infection], [excessive availability of facilities], [a complete health assessment])

#mcq(16, [Health behaviour can be influenced by], [a person's name alone], [motivation alone in every case], [one test result alone], [income, housing, education and access to services])

#mcq(17, [Which is an environmental influence on health?], [availability of safe water], [a person's initials], [a game score], [a single inherited gene only])

#mcq(18, [An inherited factor is best described as], [a facility built by a school], [a characteristic passed through biological inheritance], [a local water supply], [a handwashing station])

#mcq(19, [A risk factor is], [associated with a change in the probability of an outcome], [a guarantee that other factors do not matter], [proof that every exposed person will become ill], [a complete individual diagnosis])

#mcq(20, [A protective factor may], [serve as a complete diagnosis], [guarantee that illness is impossible], [eliminate all other influences], [reduce risk or support wellbeing])

#mcq(21, [A study finds an association between a factor and an outcome. This alone], [shows that no further evidence is needed], [proves every individual case has that cause], [rules out alternative explanations], [does not prove the cause of every individual case])

#mcq(22, [Health promotion can include], [only treatment after illness], [education together with changes that improve access], [only a competition score], [information without any consideration of barriers])

#mcq(23, [Which intervention addresses both knowledge and access?], [assume every learner has identical resources], [teach handwashing but remove the station], [install a station but prohibit its use], [teach handwashing and maintain a soap-and-water station])

#mcq(24, [A trustworthy health claim should be evaluated for], [number of shares alone], [confidence of wording alone], [attractive packaging alone], [source, evidence, date and relevance])

#mcq(25, [An advertisement promises one product cures every disease. The best response is to], [stop prescribed treatment immediately], [share it without verification], [check reliable evidence and seek appropriate advice], [assume the claim is true because it is confident])

#mcq(26, [A study guide should be used as], [a reason to ignore severe symptoms], [educational information, not a replacement for individual assessment], [a definitive diagnosis for any symptom], [a replacement for emergency services])

#mcq(27, [Persistent or concerning symptoms should be], [treated by copying an unrelated person's prescription], [diagnosed solely from a diagram], [ignored in every case], [discussed with an appropriately qualified professional])

#mcq(28, [Severe symptoms may require], [a sports score], [waiting indefinitely without assessment], [an unverified online cure], [urgent help according to local emergency procedures])

#mcq(29, [Respecting privacy in health matters helps], [eliminate the need for clinical care], [guarantee that no illness occurs], [replace informed consent], [protect dignity and support trust])

#mcq(30, [Stigma about illness can], [guarantee access to treatment], [discourage people from seeking support], [eliminate social barriers], [replace accurate information])

#mcq(31, [Which statement about appearance and health is most accurate?], [Appearance alone is not a complete health assessment], [Body size alone gives a complete diagnosis], [A person's clothing determines health status], [Appearance always identifies every condition])

#mcq(32, [A protective school environment could include], [accessible water, soap and safe sanitation], [facilities that pupils are forbidden to use], [no maintenance of toilets], [unclean water presented as safe])

#mcq(33, [Which example is primarily a physical aspect of health?], [body function and physical condition], [social support alone], [relationships and belonging only], [a person's membership in a club])

#mcq(34, [Which example is primarily a social aspect of health?], [a pulse count], [the name of a bone], [supportive relationships], [blood-clotting function])

#mcq(35, [Which example is primarily related to mental wellbeing?], [the definition of an artery], [the size of a relay zone], [coping with stress and seeking support], [the location of the tibia])

#mcq(36, [An individual health decision may be constrained by], [cost and availability of care], [a fixed rule that resources never matter], [a match result], [knowledge alone in every situation])

#mcq(37, [A community health message is stronger when it], [acknowledges barriers and offers practical support], [ignores the audience's circumstances], [blames everyone who lacks a resource], [promises that one action prevents all disease])

#mcq(38, [When reviewing a health source, an older publication], [is always current by definition], [may need checking against current guidance], [proves a claim without evidence], [always applies unchanged to every individual])

#mcq(39, [Which is a reasonable response to uncertainty about a treatment?], [change the treatment solely on an anonymous claim], [avoid asking questions], [consult an appropriately qualified professional], [assume all advice applies identically to everyone])

#mcq(40, [The relationship between knowledge and opportunity is best described as], [access replaces the need for accurate information], [both can influence whether healthy practices are possible], [facilities are irrelevant to all behaviour], [knowledge automatically removes every barrier])

